      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Brookneal, founded in 1802, sits where trails crossed the Staunton River, becoming a historic crossroads.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.co.campbell.va.us/377/County-History",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Campbell County was settled in 1736, incorporated in 1781, and lies in Virginia’s south‑central Piedmont foothills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.co.campbell.va.us/377/County-History",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Scotch‑Irish Presbyterians first settled the area in the late 1730s, establishing the Hat Creek community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.co.campbell.va.us/377/County-History",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Tobacco drove Campbell County’s early economy, with farmers cultivating the crop for generations.",
